```python
def euler_characteristic(triangles):
    vertices = {v for t in triangles for v in t}
    edges = set()
    for a, b, c in triangles:
        edges |= {frozenset((a, b)), frozenset((b, c)), frozenset((a, c))}
    return len(vertices) - len(edges) + len(triangles)
```

The tetrahedron gives $4 - 6 + 4 = 2$, the six-vertex $\R P^2$ gives $6 - 15 + 10 = 1$, the torus $9 - 27 + 18 = 0$. By Theorem 10 these numbers are $b_0 - b_1 + b_2$, independent of the triangulation.
